head sgi-mgras
# The IRIX 6.5.30 X server reading two pixels through the raster
# engine's data port while oglsnoop showed the pixel under the pointer,
# from run irix-20260930T234501-dc3029 (QEMU sgi-origami-mgras-image-
# paths at b0c49a11de, four-node Origin 2000, SI). Kept: the kernel's
# switch to the server's context 0x237a with its captured 63-word image,
# in the handshake gl-pixels-rectwrite.replay uses, and the server's
# read from its RESTATUS poll to its restore of XYWIN. Added: a
# public-port paint of the two pixels the read covers, columns 640 and
# 641 of screen row 512, in colours whose data-port words are
# 0x332211 and 0x665544. The capture's model answered both reads with
# zero and logged them unsupported; the reads here carry the words the
# box holds.
